.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
Every frame is untrusted input: headers are checked before any
allocation, CBOR bodies are decoded with fixed limits on size, depth and
item count, and only definite-length, tag-free CBOR with integer keys is
accepted.
.Pp
Plaintext must be requested explicitly.
A
.Dv CBL_LF_PROXY
listener believes the address in the PROXY header, so it must be
reachable only through the proxy; the header never makes a peer
authenticated.
